     <section anchor="changes-from-rfc-7810" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-appendix.a">
       <name slugifiedName="name-changes-from-rfc-7810">Changes from RFC 7810</name>
-      <t indent="0" pn="section-appendix.a-1">Errata ID 5293 (https://www.rfc-editor.org/errata/eid5293) correctly
+      <t indent="0" pn="section-appendix.a-1">Errata ID 5293 (<eref target="https://www.rfc-editor.org/errata/eid5293" brackets="none"/>) correctly
 identified that in <xref target="RFC7810" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC7810"/> the length associated with the following
 sub-TLVs did not match the figures associated with each:</t>
-      <t indent="0" pn="section-appendix.a-2"><artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt=""><![CDATA[
-   37    Unidirectional Residual Bandwidth
-]]></artwork>
-</t>
-      <t indent="0" pn="section-appendix.a-3"><artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt=""><![CDATA[
-   38    Unidirectional Available Bandwidth
-]]></artwork>
-</t>
-      <t indent="0" pn="section-appendix.a-4"><artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt=""><![CDATA[
-   39    Unidirectional Utilized Bandwidth
-]]></artwork>
-</t>
-      <t indent="0" pn="section-appendix.a-5">The length specified was 4, which did not include the RESERVED field
+      <dl newline="false" spacing="normal" indent="6" pn="section-appendix.a-2">
+        <dt pn="section-appendix.a-2.1">37</dt>
+        <dd pn="section-appendix.a-2.2">Unidirectional Residual Bandwidth</dd>
+        <dt pn="section-appendix.a-2.3">38</dt>
+        <dd pn="section-appendix.a-2.4">Unidirectional Available Bandwidth</dd>
+        <dt pn="section-appendix.a-2.5">39</dt>
+        <dd pn="section-appendix.a-2.6">Unidirectional Utilized Bandwidth</dd>
+      </dl>
+      <t indent="0" pn="section-appendix.a-3">The length specified was 4, which did not include the RESERVED field
 shown in the figures.  Subsequent investigation revealed that some
 implementations had used the specified length (4) and omitted the
 RESERVED field while other implementations included the specified
 RESERVED field and used a length of 5.</t>
-      <t indent="0" pn="section-appendix.a-6">Because these different implementation choices are not interoperable,
+      <t indent="0" pn="section-appendix.a-4">Because these different implementation choices are not interoperable,
 it was decided that a bis version should be generated to resolve this
 ambiguity.</t>
-      <t indent="0" pn="section-appendix.a-7">The choice made here is to omit the unused RESERVED field from these
+      <t indent="0" pn="section-appendix.a-5">The choice made here is to omit the unused RESERVED field from these
 sub-TLVs and use the length of 4.  This matches the corresponding
 advertisements specified in the equivalent OSPF TE specification
 <xref target="RFC7471" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC7471"/> and the corresponding BGP - Link State (BGP-LS)
 specification <xref target="RFC8571" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC8571"/>.</t>
-      <t indent="0" pn="section-appendix.a-8">Some minor editorial corrections have also been made.</t>
-      <t indent="0" pn="section-appendix.a-9">Errata ID 5486 (https://www.rfc-editor.org/errata/eid5486) identified
+      <t indent="0" pn="section-appendix.a-6">Some minor editorial corrections have also been made.</t>
+      <t indent="0" pn="section-appendix.a-7">Errata ID 5486 (<eref target="https://www.rfc-editor.org/errata/eid5486" brackets="none"/>) identified
 that in <xref target="RFC7810" section="4.6" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedLink="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7810#section-4.6" derivedContent="RFC7810"/> the definition of available
 bandwidth on bundled links used a circular definition, i.e., it used
 &quot;sum of the component link available bandwidths&quot; when it should have
 used &quot;sum of the component link residual bandwidths&quot;.  This has been
 corrected and clarified.</t>
     </section>
